{na} is a wide-scope negative, that is, its scope is the entire bridi in 
which it occurs,
regardless of where it occurs in that bridi.  And wide-scope includes also 
the prenex.
Thus {da na broda} = {na da broda}= {da broda na}={na su'o da zo'u da broda}. 
 
For a negation whose place makes a difference, use {naku.  So the above = 
{naku su'o da zo'u da broda}={ro da zo'u naku da broda}= {ro da naku broda}

           

